**CLI contract adjustment.** The previous parser returned on the first option seen, so `--help --bogus` would have exited 0. The plan below changes `src/cli.ts` to record a help request but keep scanning, so any unknown option exits 1 with usage on stderr regardless of where a help flag appears. A new test covers both orderings, and the UX canon states the rule. Everything else (gates, paths, sources, host envelopes, order, hashes) is unchanged. The rewritten content lines were checked against the same guard rules as before; they introduce no segment beginning with a runner name.

## Gates

| Slot | Portable configured command | Rationale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| lint | `none` | no linter installed by the generator or archetype; absence recorded in CODE-STYLE |
| types | `npm run typecheck` | package script `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` over `src` and `test` |
| unit | `node --test` | archetype testConventions; two node:test files |
| integration | `node dist/cli.js --help` | archetype built-CLI smoke check |
| build | `npm run build` | package script `tsup` per post-steps |
| e2e | `none` | no browser, service, or external surface to drive |
| emit | `env TSX_DISABLE_CACHE=1 node --import tsx roadmap/lib/emit.ts` | emitted roadmap tooling requires tsx; cache disabled across the unit boundary |

Each non-none gate runs separately as `cd '<scratch>' && /home/patrik/.local/bin/capbuild --env npm_config_cache=<scratch>/.npm-cache --env npm_config_logs_dir=<scratch>/.npm-logs <configured command>`, defaults and lock retained. `roadmap config check` and the selected comparator `node scripts/check-readme-catalog.mjs --project-root .` run raw, once each.

